{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And perform yibbum with her.</b> Its meaning: after you are the yavama (levir), perform the yibbum (levirate duty), and this is [the sense of] \"go in to your brother's wife.\" In the section \"When brothers dwell together\" (Deuteronomy 25:5) I will elaborate a little, if HaShem prolongs my days until I reach there."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 38, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:47:21.355682887Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}